Package: chorusR
Title: R Wrappers Around the 'chorus' Genomic Oracle Toolkit
Version: 0.0.6
Authors@R: person("Vincent", "Carey", email = "stvjc@channing.harvard.edu",
    role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Thin R wrappers that drive the Python 'chorus' package
    (<https://github.com/pinellolab/chorus>) via system2() calls into its
    per-oracle conda/mamba environments, rather than an in-process bridge
    such as 'reticulate'. Each oracle's forward pass runs isolated in its
    own environment already (this is how chorus itself works), so shelling
    out to a script and reading back a CSV is a natural fit and avoids
    tying the R session's process to a specific Python environment.
    Currently wraps two oracles: AlphaGenome and Cherimoya (CATv1), both
    via mQTL chromatin-concordance scoring scripts shipped in the chorus
    repository.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
Imports:
    utils
Suggests:
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
